    "standardized_narrative": "Gross claims outstanding reduced marginally from GBP 830.4m at 1 January 2019 to GBP 821.6m at 31 December 2019 (a GBP 8.8m net release). The movement largely reflects mixed prior-year development driven by favourable claims development and reinsurance recoveries, offset by adverse deterioration on certain 2018 large losses (notably Typhoon Jebi and the Lurssen Shipyard loss) while other 2018 wildfire exposures (Camp and Woolsey) improved. The Syndicate notes material gross exposures to a number of 2018 and 2019 catastrophe events but limited net exposure due to the reinsurance programme.",
